WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.700
DQN.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.550
This is how Q-learning learned to play Atari.

3
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.533
It took two tricks to make it work.

4
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:10.000
A Q-table needs one row per state.

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.506
But an Atari frame is two hundred ten by one hundred sixty pixels.

6
00:00:14.506 --> 00:00:17.693
That is thirty three thousand six hundred numbers.

7
00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:18.267
Hopeless.

8
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:25.067
A deep Q-network replaces the table with a neural network that generalizes across states.

9
00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:28.013
But naive Q-learning with a net diverges.

10
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:33.500
Samples arrive correlated, and the target contains the very network you are updating.

11
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.700
Here is the loop.

12
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.833
The agent acts, and every transition is stored in a large buffer.

13
00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.333
We train on random minibatches from it.

14
00:00:42.633 --> 00:00:46.067
They update the Q-network, which then picks the next actions.

15
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:52.233
DeepMind's papers fixed both problems, and those two fixes are the whole exam.

16
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:57.467
The replay buffer breaks correlation, and reuses each experience many times.

17
00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:04.367
The target network is a frozen copy, synced every N steps, so the target holds still long enough to be learned.

18
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.367
Here is DQN on CartPole.

19
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.967
The buffer size sets the replay buffer.

20
00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:13.967
The target update interval sets how often the frozen copy syncs.

21
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.467
Ablate either trick and watch the reward curve collapse.

22
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:22.733
CartPole is the hello world with the same shape as attitude control.

23
00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:28.000
The state is continuous, the corrections are discrete, and doing nothing is unstable.

24
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.233
Log q-values and reward to your tracking server.

25
00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:34.903
Then the cubesat sim trains with the identical script.

26
00:01:34.903 --> 00:01:36.900
Only the environment is swapped.

27
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.909
Let's recap.

28
00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:41.000
A network replaces the Q-table.

29
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.667
The replay buffer decorrelates the data.

30
00:01:43.967 --> 00:01:46.933
The target network stops the estimate chasing itself.

31
00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.393
Same Q-learning, just deep.

32
00:01:49.393 --> 00:01:50.433
Next up: PPO.
